The function is already minimal, so this is only a small cleanup with the same behavior. It copies `profile` and `profileIndex` into locals, so each member is loaded once, and marks the invalid path as the unlikely one.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (idx >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[idx].num;
}
```